        "**Conclusion:** *(fill in after running — see the printed tier breakdown above)*. If the `High` tier ends up capturing roughly the worst-behaving 10–15% of clients rather than, say, half of them, the thresholds are doing their job: flagging genuine outliers instead of over-flagging everyone. If the split looks off (e.g. almost no one lands in `Medium`, or `High` captures 40%+ of clients), that's a sign the cutoffs need adjusting — change the numbers in `_risk_level()` in `src/client_risk.py` and re-run this cell.\n"
