        "## 6. End-to-End Pipeline Sanity Check\n",
        "\n",
        "Trace a handful of real invoices through the full pipeline — overdue detection → tier classification — and eyeball whether the output makes sense.\n"
      ],
      "id": "pzqXJg6zODqG"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "J6eCQqjlODqG"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "check_date = df[\"DueDate\"].quantile(0.6).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n",
        "open_df = get_open_invoices(df, check_date)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"As of {check_date}: {len(open_df)} invoices were open, {open_df['IsOverdue'].sum()} overdue.\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "sample = open_df[open_df[\"IsOverdue\"]].sort_values(\"DaysOverdue\", ascending=False).head(8).copy()\n",
        "sample[\"Tier\"] = sample[\"DaysOverdue\"].apply(lambda d: reminder_tier(int(d)))\n",
        "sample[[\"customerID\", \"invoiceNumber\", \"InvoiceAmount\", \"DaysOverdue\", \"Tier\"]]\n"
      ],
      "id": "J6eCQqjlODqG"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BxFJiCK7ODqG"
      },
      "source": [
        "**QA checklist — confirm manually:**\n",
        "- [ ] Invoices with more `DaysOverdue` get equal-or-firmer tiers than ones with fewer (monotonic).\n",
        "- [ ] No invoice shows `IsOverdue = True` with a due date in the future relative to the snapshot.\n",
        "- [ ] Amounts and customer IDs match what's in the raw CSV for a couple of spot-checked rows.\n",
        "\n",
        "If all three hold, the core pipeline is trustworthy going into the demo.\n"
